lan movement: Link starts around x=128,y=150 (screen center-bottom). The cave entrance is up and to the left. Let me walk left then up.\n\nI'll play input: left for ~60 frames, up for ~120 frames, screenshot.\n\nBut careful about walking off screen edges: going left might scroll to another screen! The cave is on this screen though. Let's do it gradually with screenshots.\n\nActually a cleaner approach to the whole task: maybe I don't need to leave this screen. Let me reconsider whether there's a way to gain a rupee here.\n\nHold on — the old man's cave: in the US version, the first cave has the old man offering the sword. There's no rupee.\n\nAlternatively, the \"rupee\" count could be changed by writing a value... no, that's circular.\n\nOK, let's just adventure. Step 1: get sword. Step 2: find a bush with a rupee, or find rupees on the ground (some screens have 5 rupees pattern? no).\n\nActually! There's a much better source: the starting screen in Zelda has a cave with an old man, and in the *second quest* something else. But also, on the overworld there are screens with a \"money-making game\" (the 10-rupee cave with the old man who says \"Pay me and I'll talk\"?). Not near.\n\nAlternatively — bombs: there's a cave near the start (\"Take any one you want\"? no that's later).\n\nHmm, let me think about known Zelda geometry. The first screen is at overworld position (7,7)? Link's start is the screen with the cave to the north containing the sword. Adjacent screens: north of the start screen is the screen with the sword cave? Actually the sword cave IS on the start screen (the cave entrance is right there at the top-left of the starting screen). You walk up into it.\n\nAfter getting the sword, the nearest bush: I recall on the screen just west of the start there are bushes? Not sure.\n\nActually, a very reliable rupee source: cutting the bushes on the screen where you start... Hmm.\n\nWait, another thought: The HUD rupee display. Maybe there are rupees obtainable by pushing a rock? No.\n\nLet's just do it: get the sword, then wander and cut bushes until a rupee drops.\n\nActually, wait. There's an even simpler approach for finding ALL four counters without needing to change each: use the fact that I can read memory and write. I can find the rupee address via differential (needs a rup","truncated":true}
