k takes damage, the tiles change. I could find which RAM byte controls it by... no, still the redraw issue.\n\nOK, trace it is. Let me do the PPU write trace.\n\nActually — hmm, wait. Let me reconsider using `search_memory` on PRG ROM for the HUD code. The HUD routine is probably a known pattern... no.\n\nOK, let me just do the PPU trace. Go.\n\nActually, I realize there might be an even simpler approach: **`trace_writes` mode=read on the RAM page $0600-$06FF during the HUD update.** Hmm, no.\n\nLet me do the PPU trace.\n\nHmm, but wait: tracing PPU nametable writes for 60 frames while just standing — will the game write to the nametable at all? Probably only during scrolling. Let me include some movement.\n\nLet me set up: trace_writes with mem_type ppu, address 0x2000, length 0x400, frames 120, and simultaneously... hmm, trace_writes runs frames itself but doesn't take input. The game will just idle.\n\nDuring idle on the start screen, the game might not write to the nametable. Hmm.\n\nLet me instead trace PPU writes while on a screen where the HUD updates... \n\nHmm, actually the trace_writes tool says \"the game must actually perform the write during the window, so trigger the event (resume, play, or reset) first\". So I should first start an action; but trace_writes runs its own frames.\n\nHmm. Let me think: I can use play_input to start damage, and then immediately trace? The window is 60 frames by default; the trace starts when I call it and runs frames without input.\n\nHmm. So I need an event that happens without input during the trace window. \n\nIdea: **get Link into a state where he's continuously taking damage** (standing in the middle of enemies), then call trace_writes.\n\nThat's feasible: go to the enemy screen, stand still (he takes hits), then trace PPU writes.\n\nHmm, but he'd die.\n\nAlternatively, put Link somewhere the HUD updates periodically... \n\nHmm, actually: the HUD in Zelda might update every frame (redrawing the digits continuously). Let me just trace PPU writes on the nametable for 60 frames while idle on the start screen and see what happens.\n\nLet me do it. If the trace shows nametable writes, I can find the copy routine.\n\nLet me run trace_writes(ppu, 0x2000, 0x400, 60 frames).\n\nHmm, the emulator is paused. trace_writes is refused while paused. Let me resume first.\n\nLet me resume, then trace."}
